  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "The velocity $v$ at time $t$ of a particle $P$ moving in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nv(t)=\u27e8t(6t-4),\\,12{t}^{3}\u27e9.\n$$\n\nGiven that the particle is at the position $(20,30)$ when $t=2,$ calculate the components of the position vector of $P$ at time $t.$\n\n$r(t)=\u27e8${{field-1}}$,\\,3{t}^{4}-18\\,\u27e9$",
  "worked_solution": "To compute the position vector, we need to integrate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \u27e8t(6t-4),\\,12{t}^{3}\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\u27e8\\int t(6t-4)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int 12{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e82{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}+{C}_{1},\\,3{t}^{4}+{C}_{2}\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $r(2)=\u27e820,30\u27e9.$ Substituting $t=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(2) & =\u27e82(2)^{3}-2(2)^{2}+{C}_{1},\\,3(2)^{4}+{C}_{2}\u27e9 \\\\ \u27e820,30\u27e9 & =\u27e88+{C}_{1},48+{C}_{2}\u27e9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso we must have ${C}_{1}=12$ and ${C}_{2}=-18.$ Therefore, the position vector is\n\n$$\nr(t)=\u27e82{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}+12,\\,3{t}^{4}-18\u27e9.\n$$",
